}

{
  "answer": "yes",
  "explanation": "Flat surgical face masks have been shown to significantly reduce the number of coronavirus-carrying droplets that mask wearers release into the surrounding air. Studies have demonstrated that these masks are effective at blocking respiratory droplets, which are the primary mode of transmission for the coronavirus, thereby reducing the risk of spreading the virus to others [1][2]. The use of surgical masks as a source control measure has been supported by evidence indicating a substantial decrease in the emission of virus-laden droplets when masks are worn by infected individuals [1][2]."
}

