  "explanation": "High levels of interleukin-6 (IL-6) have been associated with an increased risk of respiratory failure and death, particularly in the context of severe infections such as COVID-19. Elevated IL-6 is a marker of hyperinflammation and cytokine release syndrome, both of which can contribute to the progression of respiratory distress and multi-organ failure. Clinical studies have demonstrated that patients with higher IL-6 levels are more likely to require mechanical ventilation and have a higher mortality rate compared to those with lower IL-6 levels [1][2]. Therefore, monitoring IL-6 levels can be useful in predicting the severity and potential outcomes of respiratory illnesses."
